{"c":[{"id":"88157b71ed581d98","sum":"Helper: new script env names go in privacy-gate.ts processEnv()/HELPER_ONLY_ENV; await PageFocus.moved; diff guard-adversary vs base before loosening a guard; askValues needed in hello; MAX_WAYS 8, optionIs, visit-capped generation; close page sessions before shutdown.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"90e1c122d2365aa7","sum":"New helper script env names go in privacy-gate.ts processEnv()/HELPER_ONLY_ENV. Await PageFocus.moved in tests. Before loosening a fill guard, diff guard-adversary --verifier vs base. Value questions need askValues in hello; realfill-asks scores AskAsks.fallback as automatic.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"efc720c8ec4faf9a","sum":"host-env.test.ts scans only helper/src for process.env; privacy-gate.ts reads its gate names via processEnv() and HELPER_ONLY_ENV, so new script env names go there. Tests can await PageFocus.moved; EngineSession.onFocus discards that promise.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T094208Z-4d056099840ba76b","text":"host-env.test.ts scans only helper/src for process.env; helper/scripts/privacy-gate.ts still reads its build-gate names (CARET_INTERNAL_BUILD, CARET_*PRIVACY_RESOURCE) through processEnv() and HELPER_ONLY_ENV, so new script env names go there too.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T100347Z-137d3d2067c38ff7","text":"Tests can await PageFocus.moved for the walk/focus completion; EngineSession.onFocus discards that promise.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"49be5dc02d9c236a","sum":"G36: before loosening a fill guard, diff guard-adversary --verifier accepts vs base; oneOfSeveral blocks role-labelled people's phones. VS1: value questions reach only hellos declaring askValues beside askChoices; realfill-asks scores AskAsks.fallback as the automatic result.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T103008Z-ae509cb3a9a659fb","text":"G36: before loosening a fill guard, diff guard-adversary --verifier accept attempts vs base; oneOfSeveral also blocks role-labelled people's phones (recruiter: Wren Ng, ...). page-w3 1f flaked once in the full fast suite, passes alone.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T103634Z-919e960bf3dcead3","text":"VS1: value questions reach only consumers whose hello declares askValues beside askChoices; realfill-asks scores a value question's AskAsks.fallback as the automatic result and its scripted picks as 'after pick'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"5dd3dcb4d8abfb74","sum":"VS1/helper: Disclosure caps at MAX_WAYS 8 (rebuilt minted requests need 'plan' shape); Ask value options state exact outputs (builders.ts optionIs); generation stops at MAX_GENERATOR_VISITS, not time; close page sessions before Helper.shutdown/Store.close.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"84a4af324deddcaf","sum":"VS1: Disclosure composes at most MAX_WAYS (8) ways; past that a text carries every reason, so a request rebuilt from verifier-minted parts needs 'plan' in its shape slot. Ask value options state exact outputs; stand-ins match them with builders.ts optionIs.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T103634Z-c66a1e426ad50081","text":"VS1: Disclosure composes at most MAX_WAYS (8) ways; past that a text carries every reason of its parts, so a request rebuilt after the verifier minted its parts as plan text needs 'plan' in its shape slot.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T103634Z-ffaa923aad520f1c","text":"VS1: an Ask's value options state exact outputs ('Proposed value: \"…\". Source: …'); test stand-ins match them with test/builders.ts optionIs, while a fill on focus keeps its quoted-candidate criteria.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"78a720eef0312ba1","sum":"Candidate generation stops at MAX_GENERATOR_VISITS, not elapsed time (no budgetMs or generator clock); a visit-cap stop still marks a partial window cut. Tests wiring page sessions into Helper close them before Helper.shutdown and Store.close.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T122806Z-20adf579b39b18f9","text":"Candidate generation stops at MAX_GENERATOR_VISITS, not elapsed time; no setGeneratorClock, budgetMs or --generator-clock override remains. stats.ms is diagnostic, and a visit-cap stop still marks a partial window cut.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T131449Z-7a0add213d3fc6e0","text":"Tests that wire page sessions into Helper must close those sessions before Helper.shutdown and Store.close; a scheduled trailing walk otherwise reaches a closed store.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0e934890a2410f1d","sum":"Source choices use windowUnit/whole units with source-naming Asks; note-unit lacks editable labels. GhostFit fits before publish/Tab; page fixes replace units, never AX. h13 hardcodes v2/host. SMAppService drops args; launchctl setenv test hooks/replay before open.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"2cf1dc4e6316fecf","sum":"realfill-asks seals before canned replies (FillTrace.owns false); no trace oracle rules. Unit choices need source-naming Asks/whole units; use windowUnit, not unlabeled note-unit. source_notes <=1200. GhostFit fits before publish/Tab; page fixes replace units, never AX.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"71e3e7853f09b491","sum":"Oracle and choices: realfill-asks seals requests before the canned oracle answers, so FillTrace.owns(req) is false there; keep oracle rules off the trace. A source-supported choice needs its whole unit sent, so only Asks naming the source window get unit-based choices.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T143933Z-2d2e0e57729d25b3","text":"realfill-asks seals each request before the canned oracle answers it, so FillTrace.owns(req) is false there: the oracle reads fill questions by their text on the scoreboard but by the trace in the vs1 kit (runB31). Don't make oracle rules depend on the trace.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T143933Z-70fb13e0b1aaff9c","text":"v2/choices: a source-supported choice needs its whole unit sent; a TextEdit note never fits an Ask that does not name it (prose share keeps half back), so only Asks naming the source window get unit-based choices. The user's request is always a basis.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"44883686663002a4","sum":"note-unit.unitText omits editable labels; choices use windowUnit. Sealed source_notes cap notes at 1200 chars (OutOfShape). GhostOverlay/PageInlineMachine publish GhostFit.wordsThatFit, so Tab takes drawn text; page fixes use pageInsert.replace units, never AX.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T160920Z-9fcd651bc6963d88","text":"Owner notes (note-unit.ts unitText) omit an editable field's label, so an owner judgement never sees 'Do not use' over a value; choices use windowUnit (title plus every shown text of the page) instead. Sealed source_notes cap each note at 1200 chars and throw OutOfShape above it.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261009T034106Z-c7a9a6930e557ee3","text":"Ghost text offers are fitted before publish (GhostOverlay.inlineText, PageInlineMachine.offer via GhostFit.wordsThatFit), so Tab takes exactly what is drawn; a page fix replaces before the caret with pageInsert.replace (units), never via AX.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"70e132a2c654a0a3","sum":"h13 requires caret-v2-host/v2/host; copy harness for other branches. swift-typecheck needs 7 GiB; low-disk HostCore: emit ScreenCore then typecheck. SMAppService drops args: launchctl setenv CARET_TEST_HOOKS/CARET_GHOST_REPLAY. onboarding-progress.json beside settings.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ed334c8ae8fc83ed","sum":"h13 VM hardcodes caret-v2-host and v2/host commits; other branches need a harness copy. swift-typecheck needs ~7 GiB free. Team-signed Caret.app hands off to SMAppService, dropping args; in VM set CARET_TEST_HOOKS/CARET_GHOST_REPLAY via launchctl setenv before open.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261009T034106Z-ca16ffafb65f3efc","text":"The h13 VM harness hardcodes caret-v2-host and requires the commit on v2/host; another branch needs its own harness copy. swift-typecheck refuses below about 7 GiB free disk.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261009T035706Z-bf989410ed1cf336","text":"PX1: an opened team-signed Caret.app hands off to its SMAppService agent, which drops launch arguments; in the VM pass CARET_TEST_HOOKS/CARET_GHOST_REPLAY to the agent with launchctl setenv before open.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"728708ae62c328b3","sum":"Disk-blocked CaretHostCore: emit CaretScreenCore module then swiftc -typecheck (~10 s/2 MB). Onboarding copy: CaretHost/Onboarding/OnboardingCopy.swift; resume/coach state: onboarding-progress.json beside settings; guide uses .floating beside System Settings.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261009T035706Z-f12bef9f03696e08","text":"PX1: CaretHostCore imports only CaretScreenCore, so swiftc -emit-module of CaretScreenCore plus swiftc -typecheck of CaretHostCore checks it in ~10 s with ~2 MB disk when heavy builds are disk-blocked.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261009T035707Z-e1b452775b82ff9a","text":"PX1 onboarding: copy lives in CaretHost/Onboarding/OnboardingCopy.swift; progress (resume step, coach slip shown) in onboarding-progress.json beside the settings file; the guide frame floats at .floating beside System Settings.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
